    <string name="native_about_tagline" formatted="false">Your questions.\nYour phone. Your AI.</string>
    <string name="native_about_bio" formatted="false">Offline AI research on your phone. Answers with sources, no signal needed. Open source (MIT).</string>
    <string name="native_about_post_why" formatted="false">When AI lives only on someone else\'s server, whoever runs it holds a switch.\n\nWe\'d rather no one did. So the model lives on your phone, and no server receives your questions.</string>
    <string name="native_about_post_offline" formatted="false">BoarLite has no internet access at all, so airplane mode is fine: it answers from the library on your phone and shows the articles it used.</string>
    <string name="native_about_post_receipt" formatted="false">Every answer shows how long it took and which articles it used.</string>
    <string name="native_about_post_budget" formatted="false">Before a model loads, BoarLite checks that it fits your phone\'s memory.</string>
    <string name="native_about_post_open" formatted="false">Open source, MIT. The code, the model list and the scripts that build the knowledge packs:</string>
    <string name="native_about_post_verify" formatted="false">News comes only from these addresses. Check the address before you download anything that says it is BoarLite.</string>
